    "source": "Already mid-action, Pip the rabbit tries to place one sticky note on the toy cabinet's empty front panel, but it clings to Pip's fingertip while the cabinet stays untouched. Pip tries to peel the note away with the free hand, but it splits into two notes, one on each hand. Pip tries to press both notes onto the cabinet, but they spring back and double into four notes. Pip tries to push the four notes off against the cabinet door edge, but they split into eight and cover Pip's arms and face. Pip sees the four-to-eight change finish, realizes that every removal or transfer attempt multiplies the notes, deliberately stops struggling, and turns the still note-covered face toward the mirror. Pip remains covered until a sneeze scatters the notes onto the cabinet. Pip is relieved, but the cabinet remains messy.",
    "objective": "Propose a materially stronger, natural 15-second ABSURD_PHYSICS story for SEEDANCE_2_0_MINI, image2video, 480p, 9:16. Preserve Pip the rabbit, the sticky-note/cabinet premise, the existing multiplication rule and the final sneeze leaving Pip relieved beside a messy cabinet. Other source events/order are revision proposals, not automatically approved facts. Improve the first visible promise, distinct viewer-visible consequences and natural pacing; reduce artificial strategy density and overloaded final seconds. Avoid thin-object precision where possible; report concept unsuitability rather than disguising generator risk. Compare real creative merit, not numerical rule coverage. No audience or render claims.",
